truth-suite

"Truth suite is the project source of truth, compounded from true statements made by a human in their natural language. With an accompanying truth harness to automate the process of; checking, disputing, building with, locking, maintaining the truth"

"Truth is recorded at three levels; File level, Concept level and Principle level."

"File level is where statements describe what must be true for a file or small group of files serving the same purpose. If files are grouped, they cannot have adjacent singular truth records over the same file, if this is required extract the statements from the group into the singular file."

"Of the three levels file level truth has the lower altitude, ensuring the highest fidelity of truth. An agent with a truth file can easily red/green check a file against the truth statements in the file."

"Concept level truths sit midway in abstraction, The concept can be detected in the project but may exist across many files and may not be a direct implementation."

"An example of a concept truth may be an approval process that exists across many files and appears as a status state and flow."

"Concept truths are checked across all files that they permeate into or affect in the project."

"Concepts are easily found when truth files repeat the same statement as other truth files. Extraction into a concept creates opportunity to define the concept once and in far greater depth than all the individual truth files do collectively. Concepts also allow very low-detail mentions inside a truth file, while still being entirely checkable."

"Principle level is high abstraction, but is often visible in directional overview. Principle truths often represents a universal principle that propagates throughout the project."

"Principles are found where truth statements repeatedly across many truth files or concepts, try to convey meaning that has no direct existence in a file. They do not guide layout, location, field types, data, but instead provide a purpose for the file or concept exisiting in the first place."

"Checking a principle is different from the other levels, do not try to determine a principle is followed as a red/green check. Instead let an agent with the principle, ensure that it is followed as part of a build team, trying to figure out what is built. Or in planning stages to include or disclude certain possible solutions."
